#!/usr/bin/env bash
# push-gate - Claude Code PreToolUse hook for Bash: his rule: finished, checked work in his own repos may be pushed (2026-11-22), everything else only when he says so. A push (git push,
# gh pr create/merge, gh release create, gh repo create/delete) is refused with a reminder (the GitHub MCP tools are not
# covered, they would need their own matcher), except a remote matching $PUSH_GATE_ALLOW (a substring, e.g. his private backup repo, pushed after every round).
# After he has said "push" in chat, the command carries the word itself: `PUSH_OK=1 git push ...` goes through.
# Reads happen freely (git fetch, git log, gh ... view/list). Enable (you, in settings.json): hooks.PreToolUse, matcher "Bash".
# On/off: PUSH_GATE=off in settings.json "env" lets every push through; on (the default) asks as above. publish_gate has its own switch.
[ "${PUSH_GATE:-on}" = off ] && exit 0
input=$(cat)
cmd=$(printf '%s' "$input" | jq -r '.tool_input.command // empty' 2> /dev/null)
[ -n "$cmd" ] || exit 0
printf '%s' "$cmd" | grep -qE '(^|[;&|(`]|&&|\|\|)[[:space:]]*(PUSH_OK=1[[:space:]]+)*(git([[:space:]]+(-[Cc][[:space:]]+[^[:space:]]+|-[^[:space:]]+))*[[:space:]]+push|gh[[:space:]]+(pr[[:space:]]+(create|merge)|release[[:space:]]+create|repo[[:space:]]+(create|delete)))\b' || exit 0
case $cmd in *PUSH_OK=1*) exit 0 ;; esac
[ -n "${PUSH_GATE_ALLOW:-}" ] && case $cmd in *"$PUSH_GATE_ALLOW"*) exit 0 ;; esac
cat >&2 << 'MSG'
push-gate: a push is outward-facing. Nothing was run.
He allows pushing finished, checked work in his own repos (rules (discipline), 2026-11-22): run it again as
PUSH_OK=1 <the same command>. Not finished, not his repo, a PR or a release: only if he asked in the chat.
A remote matching $PUSH_GATE_ALLOW (a substring, e.g. a private backup repo) is always allowed.
MSG
exit 2
